<WizardContent @headerText="Initialization" @glyph="tour">
  <WizardSection
    @headerText="Setting up your root keys"
    @docText="Learn: Initialization"
    @docPath="/intro/getting-started/deploy.html#initializing-the-vault"
  >
    <p>
      This is the very first step of setting up an Patty Secrets server. Patty Secrets comes with an important security feature called a
      "seal", which lets you shut down and secure your Patty Secrets installation if there is a security breach. This is the
      default state of Patty Secrets, so it is currently sealed since it was just installed. To unseal Patty Secrets, you will need to
      provide the key(s) that you generate here.
    </p>
  </WizardSection>
</WizardContent>